Query templates advised by pg_plan_advice, for PostgreSQL 19.

pg_plan_advice/ holds one copy of each of the 99 PostgreSQL query
templates (the stock template, or the query_postgresql/ rewrite where
one exists) with one line inserted before every statement:

    RESET pg_plan_advice.advice; select set_config('pg_plan_advice.advice', '...', false);

The string is the generated advice of the fastest plan found for that
statement in a plan study on PostgreSQL 19beta3 at scale factor 20
(sets are kept under advice/ in the repository, with the study's
provenance).  A statement without advice gets an empty string.  The
templates are written by tools/advise-templates.sh from the plain
templates and the advice files; they are not edited by hand.

query_templates/pgsqla.tpl is the pgsql dialect with LOAD
'pg_plan_advice' before the timing insert and RESET pg_plan_advice.advice
before the timing update.  query_templates/pgsqlaea.tpl adds
auto_explain with log_extension_options = 'plan_advice', so the results
file carries each plan with the feedback on every supplied advice item
and the generated advice of the executed plan.  The dialects sit in
query_templates/ because dsqgen opens the dialect as
DIRECTORY/DIALECT.tpl.  templates-pgsqla.lst lists the advised set:

    dbt7 run -d pgsqla \
        -i "${DSHOME}/query_templates/templates-pgsqla.lst" pgsql DIR

Why set_config and not SET: SET is a keyword of the dsqgen template
grammar and cannot start a line.  Why RESET first: the set_config
statement is itself planned, and would otherwise be planned under the
previous statement's advice.

